4.0-dev (branch 010-enhanced-features-lgb):

- New experiment_v7.py: Enhanced feature set + fold-safe SMOTE + two-model
  ensemble (LightGBM + CatBoost). Extends the v6 OBIA+PB hybrid with insights
  from niwacolours/benthic-terrain-model-kaggle@002-boost-weighted-f1:
    - 6 multi-scale focal std features (bathy_std/back_std at 3/5/9 cells)
    - 2 TPI features (topographic position index at 9 and 25 cell windows)
    - 4 interaction terms (bathy×back, slope×back, roughness ratio, relief idx)
    - 4 spatial context features (x_rel/y_rel, depth_z, backscatter_z)
    - Total: 34 features (8 PB + 6 focal + 2 TPI + 4 interaction + 4 spatial +
      10 OB). Previously 18 (8 PB + 10 OB).
  Ensemble reduced to LightGBM + CatBoost (RF and XGBoost dropped — they were
  diluting the ensemble without measurable CV gain). LightGBM hyperparameters
  tuned from companion repo (n_estimators=600, lr=0.03, num_leaves=31).
  SMOTE applied fold-safe (only within CV training folds; fallback to
  RandomOverSampler when minority count < 2). ID column now uppercase 'ID'.
  CV results (6-split, 6-cluster KMeans): PB-only F1=0.5147, OB-only F1=0.3932,
  Combined F1=0.6075 (combined best; CatBoost; +0.032 vs v6 combined).
  Global Moran's I included in run report for EDA (top 12 features).
- Fixed: submission CSV 'ID' column now correctly uppercase (was lowercase
  'id' in v6, causing Kaggle submission rejection).
- New tests/unit/test_experiment_v7_features.py: 8 unit tests covering focal
  std shape/finiteness/monotonicity, TPI flatness property, bathy×back product,
  roughness ratio non-negativity, SMOTE minority class growth, combined feature
  count correctness (34 total, no duplicates), and spatial context [0-1] range.
- New docs/run-010-enhanced-features-lgb.md: run report with feature group
  table, segmentation parameters, CV F1 table, feature importances (top 15),
  and Global Moran's I per feature.
- New data/submission_v7_best.csv: 98-row submission with uppercase 'ID'.

4.0-dev (branch 009-obia-pixel-hybrid):

- New experiment_v6.py: OBIA + pixel-based hybrid classification following
  Ierodiaconou et al. (2018) Marine Geodesy DOI:10.1007/s11001-017-9338-z.
  The paper used the same Refuge Cove MBES dataset and found combined PB+OB
  achieved 83.6% OA vs 72.5% PB-only. This experiment derives 8 pixel-based
  features (depth, backscatter, slope, VRM, complexity, max curvature,
  northness, eastness) and 10 object-based features (SLIC segmentation →
  per-segment mean/std/skewness of bathy/back/VRM + pixel count).
  CV results: PB-only F1=0.5665, OB-only F1=0.3886, Combined F1=0.5758
  (combined best; CatBoost; spatial block GroupKFold 10 folds seed=42).
- New tests/unit/test_experiment_v6_features.py: 7 unit tests validating
  PB feature completeness, northness/eastness range, segment label shape
  and non-negativity, segment mean size range, OB feature completeness,
  and combined feature count of exactly 18.
- New docs/run-009-obia-pixel-hybrid.md: run report with segmentation
  parameters, per-configuration CV F1 table, and top feature importances.

4.0-dev (branch 008-gis-feature-engineering):

- New experiment_v5.py: GIS-derived feature engineering adding slope,
  backscatter zones and acoustic facies with 80/20/20 weighting on top
  of the v2 comprehensive feature set.
- Run A: raw point-sampled GIS features; Run B: zone-stratified kriging
  smoothing for test-point inference (5-zone OrdinaryKriging, spherical
  variogram, KNN fallback for small zones).
- New tests/unit/test_experiment_v5_features.py: 5 unit tests for the
  GIS feature helpers (shape, weight correctness, submission format,
  kriging no-NaN, run report completeness).
- New output files: data/submission_v5_gis_features.csv (Run A),
  data/submission_v5_gis_features_kriging.csv (Run B),
  data/submission_v5_best.csv (best of A/B).
- New docs/run-008-gis-feature-engineering.md: experiment metrics report.
  3.0-final:
- ArcGIS Pro / Python 3 support added.
- New Compare Scales of Analysis tool provides a quick approximation of the effects of scale.
- Added option in Surface Area to Planar Area to use slope-corrected Planar Area as described in DuPreez (2014).
- New Arc Chord Ratio tool which computes metrics for an area of interest as described in DuPreez (2014).
- Added new depth statistics using SciPy, Kurtosis and Interquartile range.
- New multiple scales tool to compute depth statistics and VRM at a range of scales from within a single tool.
- Extensive testing on large data, includes a block-based processor for computation on larger datasets with NumPy / SciPy operations.
- New Set Workspace tool which propagates storage settings across all tools.
- Compression is enabled for all outputs.
  3.0-rc-7: add contact sheet, VRM scale validation
  3.0-rc-6: fix broad-scale validation error, locale issue, remove unused validator.
  3.0-rc-5: fix locale issues.
  3.0-rc-4: fix missing datatypes module in Python toolbox.
  3.0-rc-3: robustness improvements to Surface Area to Planar Area tool, updated documentation, simplify VRM script.
  3.0-rc-2: Statistical Aspect tool, Excel-based classification dictionaries.
  3.0-beta-20: handle CSV files more robustly, provide clearer error messages, fix classify bug, add new Surface Area to Planar Area tool, improvements to VRM code, internal code cleanup, Excel support.
  3.0-beta-14: move model into a Python script over ModelBuilder, complete
  top-level unit tests.
  3.0-beta-13:
- fix regression with "classify benthic terrain" step in model; renamed from zoneclassification to classify @aa49aad.
